# Human-rating identity

**Doc link:** <https://github.com/brando90/judges-dont-need-psychometrics-or-corr/blob/main/.cursor/rules/human-rating-identity.mdc>

**TLDR:** Every personal human-rating Google Sheet and CSV starts with the actual `rater_name`, then stable `rater_id`.

Read `AGENTS.md`, especially “Human-rating identity and collection,” before preparing, editing, exporting or importing ratings. It contains the same project policy as `CLAUDE.md`. Apply it to every participant; preserve source ratings and archived packets, verify column-name mappings and keep active Sheets and CSV exports consistent. The shared VeriBench collection is owned by [trustworthy-theorem-judges experiment 09](https://github.com/brando90/trustworthy-theorem-judges/tree/main/experiments/09_prepare_packets_and_collect_human_ratings_start_28Sep2026); follow its identity/import workflow instead of creating a second collection.
